WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
You choose one of two photographs. The answer feels obvious.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
But imagine the picture handed back is the one you did not select.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
In a 2005 experiment, some people missed that switch.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
They could still give reasons for the face they were shown.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
The report was real. But the explanation was not a recording of their original choice.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Read the study. Keep the evidence separate from the story—especially when a product promises to change your mind.
